; CORE303 part 2 fixture: verbs enter the BENCH driver (src/bench.asm) by EXTERN 0 13,
; mode in flag 250, ISR state in flag 251. Compiled: ndrc nextdaad EN -v3 -nxtext.

; Contract (tests/core303/test_fixture.py): message 0 = BCH_MSG_LEN plain characters;
; picture 1 = 001.NX3, 256x96 at 0,0 (tilemap rows 4-15); window 0 = rows 17-30, 80
; columns; row 31 holds LOG OK/FAIL.

; Assets (SOURCES.txt): 001.NX3 (picture 1), 001.AKY (SFX 1 7), 001.WAV (SFX 1 2). No
; GAME.AKY, GAME.AYS or GAME.SFB: each arms audio at boot, and BISR then skips (STATE).

; Flag 251 is the ISR state (0 idle, 1 song, 2 SFX). audEnable sticks once audio starts,
; and text, NX3 and idle rows then skip (STATE); BTRN's gt_init calls isr_idle, so a
; session runs in this order: BTXT, BPIC, BISR, BTRN, BISM, BISS, BLOG.

; BTXT mode 1 text, BPIC mode 2 NX3, BISR/BISM/BISS mode 3 ISR idle / AKY / streamed
; SFX, BTRN mode 4 game turn, BLOG mode 5 log step.

; BTRN's turn injects "EXAMINE LAMP" (bench.asm gtLine): PRO 5's last entry answers with
; MES 3 and DONE, one window line, no location change.

/CTL
_
/VOC
BTXT   20 verb
BPIC   21 verb
BISR   22 verb
BISM   23 verb
BISS   24 verb
BTRN   25 verb
BLOG   26 verb
EXAMI  27 verb
LAMP   50 noun
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 " "
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "The bench decodes this fixed message through the Huffman reader, then prints it into the window below the picture."
/1 "BENCH DONE#n"
/2 "CORE303 BENCH FIXTURE#n"
/3 "The brass lamp is old and dented.#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/CON
/0
/OBJ
/0    0   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   WINDOW 0
        WINAT 17 0
        WINSIZE 14 80
        CLS
        MES 2
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 5
        ISDONE
        REDO
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        REDO
/PRO 5
> BTXT _  LET 250 1
          EXTERN 0 13
          MES 1
          DONE
> BPIC _  PICTURE 1
          DISPLAY 0
          LET 250 2
          EXTERN 0 13
          MES 1
          DONE
> BISR _  LET 251 0
          LET 250 3
          EXTERN 0 13
          MES 1
          DONE
> BISM _  SFX 1 7
          PAUSE 25
          LET 251 1
          LET 250 3
          EXTERN 0 13
          MES 1
          DONE
> BISS _  SFX 0 8
          SFX 1 2
          PAUSE 25
          LET 251 2
          LET 250 3
          EXTERN 0 13
          MES 1
          DONE
> BTRN _  LET 250 4
          EXTERN 0 13
          MES 1
          DONE
> BLOG _  LET 250 5
          EXTERN 0 13
          MES 1
          DONE
> EXAMI LAMP MES 3
          DONE
/END
